From: Zylos <audit>
Subject: [PATCH] emblem-fury: drop the redundant re-render that crashes weapon fusion

Round 10, domrun.mjs. fuseWeapons() ended by calling renderInventory(), which
does document.getElementById('inv-panel').innerHTML='' -- and #inv-panel appears
exactly once in the file, at that lookup. It is null, so every FUSE click threw
TypeError *after* the fusion had already been committed to player.weapons.

Effect on the player: the two weapons really are consumed and merged, then the
handler dies before the UI refreshes, so the inventory keeps showing the old
pair until it is closed and reopened.

The call is redundant as well as fatal: the FUSE button's own handler already
re-renders via renderInventoryInto(#inv-content) once fuseWeapons returns.

Verified: fuseWeapons(0,1) threw TypeError before, returns normally after, with
the fusion still applied (2 weapons -> 1).

Leaves renderInventory() (and tierClass, its only other caller) fully
unreachable -- ~110 lines of dead code. Deleting it is a separate call, not
made here.

--- a/emblem-fury.html
+++ b/emblem-fury.html
@@ -1459,7 +1459,8 @@
   fusionSelectIndices=[];
   playSound('pickupWeapon');
   announceAbility('WEAPON FUSED!','#ff0');
-  renderInventory();
+  // The caller re-renders (renderInventoryInto). renderInventory() targets
+  // #inv-panel, which this page no longer has.
 }
 
 // ── INVENTORY UI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
